# The public half of the release signing key (ed25519, PEM).
#
# Releases published by .github/workflows/release.yml are signed with the
# private half, held as the CXCG_RELEASE_SIGNING_KEY secret of the "release"
# environment. Once a key is pasted here, images built from this commit install
# only releases whose signature verifies against it, automatically or by hand.
# The key is always read from the IMAGE's own copy of this file (never from the
# data volume or a downloaded version), so a release cannot bring its own key.
#
# Until then it is empty: auto-update installs nothing (it "waits for the release
# signing key"), an admin can install a release by hand only after confirming
# that it cannot be verified, and the release workflow refuses to publish.
# To set it up once:
#   python backend/scripts/release_keygen.py
# then paste the printed "-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----" block below these comments,
# and store the private key file's contents as the CXCG_RELEASE_SIGNING_KEY secret.
# CXCG_UPDATE_PUBLIC_KEY (the PEM text) overrides this file.
